<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY BANKS IN RUSSIA LOAN DEAL FOR IKARUS BUSES.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY BANKS IN RUSSIA LOAN DEAL FOR IKARUS BUSES.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A BNP-Dresdner-led consortium of Hungarian banks said on Friday it had signed loan agreements worth $42.895 million with Russian bank Rossiisky Kredit Bank to finance the exports to Russia of 403 Hungarian Ikarus buses.</p>
<p>The consortium is made mup of BNP-Dresdner's Hungarian unit BNP-Dresdner Bank-Hungaria Rt, the Central European International Bank Limited and Eximbank. The buses will be delivered to Moscow over three years.</p>
</text>
